-- title:
--   Noetherian square-zero lifting suffices for Theta formal étaleness
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, with $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi))=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$; let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero field that is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$-algebra, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo it and every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo it. Let $G$ be a type and $fN : N \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ a morphism of schemes that is locally of finite type. Write $F(B) = ((Onr \to_{\mathcal O} B) \times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}(K_0,\pi,B)) \times G$ for $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ — a Deligne datum being a choice, for each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M \subset K_0^2$, of a $B$-submodule $\mathrm{line}(M) \subseteq B\otimes_{\mathcal O}M$ with invertible quotient, compatible with lattice inclusions and with homotheties, and nondegenerate at every prime of $B$ — with functoriality given by composition on the $Onr$-leg, span of the image under base change on lines, and the identity on $G$; and write $\hat N(B) = \{\varphi : \operatorname{Spec}B \to N \mid \varphi \text{ followed by } fN \text{ equals } \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O \to B)\}$, functorial by precomposition with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of an algebra map. Given maps $\Theta_B : F(B) \to \hat N(B)$ for all $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, natural in $\mathcal O$-algebra maps between such $B$, assume: for every Noetherian such $B$, every $\pi$-nilpotent $B_0$ and every surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $p : B \to B_0$ whose kernel has square zero (any two elements killed by $p$ multiply to $0$), each $x_0 \in F(B_0)$ and $y \in \hat N(B)$ with $\hat N(p)(y) = \Theta_{B_0}(x_0)$ admit a unique $x \in F(B)$ with $F(p)(x)=x_0$ and $\Theta_B(x)=y$. The conclusion is the same unique lifting statement with the Noetherian hypothesis on $B$ dropped.
--
--   This is the formal-étaleness clause for the comparison morphism $\Theta$ from the product of the $Onr$-rigidification, the Drinfeld (Deligne-datum) functor $\hat\Omega$ and the discrete factor $G$ to the functor of $\pi$-nilpotent points of $N$: it removes the Noetherian restriction from the unique-lifting criterion along square-zero thickenings. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld fine family and of the associated tower family.
